course: dictionary
lesson: 15360
title: A big word for sleepy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal. They appear in reports, medicine labels and grown-up books more than in everyday chat. «Somnolence» is one of them, and it means sleepiness: the heavy, drowsy feeling that makes you want to close your eyes. Look at the words around it for clues: «After a huge lunch, heavy somnolence crept over the class.» Heavy and crept tell you it is about feeling sleepy.
explain: Writers also use somnolence to describe a place. «The village lay in a hot, quiet somnolence all afternoon.» Nothing moved and nobody spoke, so the village felt sleepy and still. Hot, quiet and all afternoon are the clues.
explain: Medicine labels often use this word. A label might say «may cause somnolence», which is a warning not to drive, because you could feel too drowsy to stay alert. In everyday talk, you would just say sleepiness or drowsiness.
fact: Somnolence means sleepiness, the feeling of being drowsy and heavy.
fact: Somnolence is a formal word, so you will meet it more in writing than in speech.
fact: When it describes a place, somnolence means a sleepy, very quiet state.
fact: Simple words with the same idea are sleepiness and drowsiness.
fact: Doctors and medicine labels use somnolence to warn that a medicine may make you sleepy.
exercise: «After a huge lunch, heavy somnolence crept over the class.» What does somnolence mean here? | Excitement before a party | A sudden rainstorm | *Sleepiness | Loud cheering in the playground
exercise: A medicine label says «may cause somnolence». What is the warning? | Read the label twice before breakfast | Drive faster than usual | *Do not drive, because you may feel too drowsy | Go swimming in the sea after the dose
exercise: Which everyday word is a simple way to say somnolence? | Hunger | Laughter | *Drowsiness | Bravery
test: «The village lay in a hot, quiet somnolence all afternoon.» What is the village like? | Crowded with tourists | Noisy and busy | *Sleepy and very still | Cold and wet
test: Which is the best synonym for somnolence in everyday talk? | Courage | Hunger | *Drowsiness | Excitement
exam: A label warns «may cause somnolence». Why should you not drive after taking the medicine? | Because the medicine makes you run faster | Because the label is written in a formal style | Because the bottle is hot | *Because the medicine can make you drowsy, so it is unsafe to drive
